This code performs the PHF and PCC optimization for molecules and Hubbard
lattices, run through the driver function below. This code contains
contributions from Carlos Jimenez-Hoyos, Yiheng Qiu, Tom Henderson, Ruiheng
Song, and Jeff Keyes.

To run first compile the PHF code by going into the PHF_fort dir
and running
 > bash makefile 
There is a MPI and no_MPI version that decides whether to use MPI
parallelization. Both use openmp. Running the makefile will produce a file
called PHF_Tools_F.*.so where * is replaced by details of your python version.
Move this file to the main directory.  A similar process can be done for the
PCC code in SUCCSD_Boson_Cmplx.

To run the code, set up an .xyz file for you geometry and a .json file
containing details of the calculation. Information on these settings can be
found in the PCC_objects.py file. An example for H2 is given. Finally, run the
code as:
 > python PCC_driver.py -s H2.json
The output should look like H2_example.out
Be sure to set the OMP_NUM_THREADS environmental variable for parallelization
